# Mermaid program flowcharts

When explaining Teach Pendant / Karel, use **one** Mermaid `flowchart` — not a rectangle chain plus a stub diamond chart.

GitHub-safe classic syntax only. Do **not** use `@{ shape: diamond }` (many Markdown hosts miss it).

## Shapes

| Kind | Shape | Syntax |
|------|--------|--------|
| Start / END | Stadium | `id(["L9 END"])` |
| Motion / assign / JMP | Rectangle | `id["L4 J PR1"]` |
| IF, WAIT timeout, SKIP | Diamond (rhombus) | `id{"L3 WAIT RI?"}` |
| DI/DO/RI/RO | Parallelogram | `id[/"L2 RO[1]=ON"/]` |
| CALL | Subroutine | `id[["L5 CALL SUB100"]]` |
| Remark / skipped | Rounded | `id("L0 remarks")` |

## Edges

| Edge | Use |
|------|-----|
| `==>` | Happy / main path |
| `-->` | Normal next instruction |
| `-.->` | Remark, optional, skipped, TIMEOUT / fault |
| ` -->|yes| ` ` -->|TIMEOUT| ` | Diamond branches |

## Line numbers

**ALWAYS** prefix executable nodes with `L` + `/MN` number from `code/solution.ls` (e.g. `L3 WAIT RI`). Ranges OK: `L4-6 CALL loop`. Collapse LEGAL remarks to one `note` node.

## Colors (copy into every diagram)

```text
classDef proc fill:#DAE8FC,stroke:#6C8EBF
classDef dec fill:#FFF2CC,stroke:#D6B656
classDef io fill:#D5E8D4,stroke:#82B366
classDef call fill:#E1D5E7,stroke:#9673A6
classDef fault fill:#F8CECC,stroke:#B85450
classDef term fill:#F5F5F5,stroke:#666666
classDef note fill:#FFFFFF,stroke:#999999,stroke-dasharray: 5 5
```

Then `class nodeId proc` (or `dec`, `io`, `call`, `fault`, `term`, `note`).

## NEVER

- One rectangle per remark line
- Two near-identical diagrams (Flowchart + empty Decisions)
- Fake diamonds on a straight program
- Plant I/O maps; placeholders only
- OEM manual paste in node labels

